  vllm-patches/          model_executor/models/mimo_v2_omni.py
                         Port of vllm-project/vllm#58235 (open at the time; single commit 3650a535): the MiMo ViT
                         window-attention sink as a null softmax logit instead of a bias on key 0.
                         vllm-58235.diff = the upstream pull request's diff (reference only, not mounted).

  vllm-patches-tools/    parser/mimo.py (new upstream file), parser/engine/registered_adapters.py,
                         reasoning/__init__.py, reasoning/mimo_engine_reasoning_parser.py,
                         tool_parsers/__init__.py, tool_parsers/mimo_tool_parser.py
                         Port of vllm-project/vllm#58019 (merged 2026-09-29 as dfc8e0f3): the `mimo` tool parser
                         keeps string arguments verbatim. Difference from upstream: no xgrammar structural tag
                         (structural_tag_model = None), because the image ships xgrammar 0.2.7 and upstream's tag
                         needs 0.2.8. vllm-58019.diff = the upstream pull request's diff (reference only).

  vllm-patches-attn2/    v1/attention/ops/triton_unified_attention_diffkv.py,
                         v1/attention/backends/triton_attn_diffkv.py
                         Our GB10 (sm_121) launch tuning of the Triton DiffKV attention (per-layer-type tiles,
                         split-KV verify, 2D sliding-window verify) and a Q.K^T split (192 = 128 + 64, no pad to
                         256). Env switches: MIMO_DIFFKV_TUNE=0 (stock launch), MIMO_DIFFKV_QK_SPLIT=0,
                         MIMO_DIFFKV_PF_FULL / _PF_SWA / _DEC_FULL / _DEC_SWA / _SEGS. Related upstream work:
                         vllm-project/vllm#58177, #59085, #58141.

  vllm-patches-fp8cfg/   model_executor/layers/quantization/utils/configs/N=*,K=4096,device_name=NVIDIA_GB10,...json
                         Four block-FP8 GEMM kernel configs (data) generated on GB10 with vLLM's own tuner
                         (benchmarks/kernels/benchmark_w8a8_block_fp8.py, see kernel-tuning/).

  vllm-patches-roce/     distributed/device_communicators/cuda_communicator.py (modified copy: a hook that routes
                         eligible TP all-reduces to mimo_roce_rd, a health check before eager all-gathers, cleanup)
                         distributed/device_communicators/mimo_roce_rd.py (NEW FILE, ours, Apache-2.0): ring-only
                         recursive doubling built from two 2-rank RoCEnante runtimes.
                         roce-rd.diff = our diff of cuda_communicator.py against the image's copy (reference only).
                         Needs b12x (https://github.com/local-inference-lab/b12x, Apache-2.0, commit
                         e4084d2eef4932e0fa06db3f7a94deb83ad132d7), which is NOT included here; the launcher mounts a
                         checkout read-only (B12X=<short sha>). The HCA pairing in mimo_roce_rd.py is hardcoded for a
                         ring cabled 0-1-2-3-0 with each node's port 0 to the next node's port 1.

The .diff files are documentation; only the paths listed in each SHA256SUMS are mounted.
